        "answer": {
          "short": "\\$39 642",
          "worked": "The taxable income is in the \\$120 001–\\$180 000 bracket.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Excess}&=147\\,500-120\\,000\\\\\\text{Excess}&=27\\,500\\\\\\text{Tax payable}&=29\\,467+0.37\\times27\\,500\\\\\\text{Tax payable}&=\\$39\\,642\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p63-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Charlie has paid tax instalments \\$860 per week. How much is this over the year?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "\\$44 720",
          "worked": "Using 52 weeks in a year:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Total instalments}&=860\\times52\\\\\\text{Total instalments}&=\\$44\\,720\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p63-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Will Charlie receive a tax refund or will he have to pay more tax?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Tax refund.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Balance}&=44\\,720-39\\,642\\\\\\text{Balance}&=\\$5078\\end{align*}$$\nThe balance is positive, so Charlie has paid too much tax and will receive a tax refund.",
